        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T00:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need both. SUITE_UCSI_PPM doesn\u0027t have the granularity of SUITE_PPM_DRIVER, which mocks functions. For example, it\u0027s difficult for SUITE_UCSI_PPM to exercise branches based on the return values from pdc_execute_ucsi_cmd without mocking it.",
      "parentUuid": "965af88e_6d9166c3",
      "revId": "a779918a0cd572a02df88d1468250a7932e19740",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8a475cf_88dbe1e4",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T00:13:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we not add `emul_` apis for PDC to return specific values?",
      "parentUuid": "4e0ea5d0_94107aa5",
      "revId": "a779918a0cd572a02df88d1468250a7932e19740",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6828ab9d_2a094174",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T01:55:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a pdc driver between a PDC emulator and ppm_driver. So, it\u0027s hard to control the return value. There is emul_pdc_set_cmd_error. This allows SUITE_UCSI_PPM to exercise a timeout (i.e. events \u003d\u003d 0) but it doesn\u0027t affect pdc_execute_ucsi_cmd, which always returns 0.\n\nFor the same reason, other pdc_* functions are hard to control.\n\nSo, I think we want to use\n* SUITE_PPM_DRIVER for the coverage (by exercising corner cases)\n* SUITE_UCSI_PPM for testing the PPM against the UCSI spec.",
      "parentUuid": "a8a475cf_88dbe1e4",
      "revId": "a779918a0cd572a02df88d1468250a7932e19740",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d944ae4b_5eee2c4b",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T17:17:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case, maybe just a naming change --\n\nSUITE_PPM_DRIVER_MOCKED\nSUITE_PPM_DRIVER\n\nIMO, my confusion is because they are both testing ppm_driver but `SUITE_UCSI_PPM` is less descriptive of what\u0027s being tested.\n\nI would also support renaming `SUITE_PPM` into `SUITE_PPM_STATE_MACHINE`.",
      "parentUuid": "6828ab9d_2a094174",
      "revId": "a779918a0cd572a02df88d1468250a7932e19740",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
